WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:13.971
Pedro zigzagged around Great-Aunt Luisa's dark front yard, holding his phone up.

2
00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:17.434
He was trying to get a stronger signal.

3
00:00:18.575 --> 00:00:22.519
Great-Aunt Luisa lived in the countryside, where there wasn't much to do.

4
00:00:24.961 --> 00:00:27.404
Pedro was staying with her for a whole month.

5
00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:32.594
"Are you taking pictures of the moon?"

6
00:00:33.054 --> 00:00:33.895
a voice called.

7
00:00:35.276 --> 00:00:37.658
Pedro spotted a girl in a neighbor's yard.

8
00:00:37.678 --> 00:00:41.442
"No. I was just trying to get a signal."

9
00:00:41.822 --> 00:00:42.983
He glanced upward.

10
00:00:44.224 --> 00:00:48.268
The nearly full moon looked much brighter than it looked at home in the city.

11
00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:50.790
The girl smiled.

12
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.251
"I'm Luna.

13
00:00:52.832 --> 00:00:54.573
Want to take a look through my telescope?"

14
00:00:56.855 --> 00:01:01.775
"Sure." Pedro walked over to where Luna had set up her telescope.

15
00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:05.538
"I've never seen the moon through a telescope before."

16
00:01:05.558 --> 00:01:09.101
"One day I'd like to see it up close."

17
00:01:10.382 --> 00:01:11.743
Luna's eyes shone.

18
00:01:11.763 --> 00:01:17.067
"My dream is to become an astronaut and explore the moon."

19
00:01:17.087 --> 00:01:20.470
"You sure like the moon a lot.

20
00:01:21.531 --> 00:01:23.812
Is it because your name means 'moon' in Spanish?"

21
00:01:24.113 --> 00:01:25.594
Pedro asked teasingly.

22
00:01:27.055 --> 00:01:27.896
Luna grinned.

23
00:01:28.528 --> 00:01:29.329
"It could be.

24
00:01:29.349 --> 00:01:32.631
Hey! There's a full moon tomorrow.

25
00:01:33.812 --> 00:01:34.873
Want to watch it with me?"

26
00:01:36.674 --> 00:01:37.795
Pedro smiled.

27
00:01:37.815 --> 00:01:44.140
"Definitely!" The next night Pedro met Luna in her yard.

28
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:49.383
"The moon is a different shape tonight," he said.

29
00:01:50.804 --> 00:01:51.725
Luna giggled.

30
00:01:51.745 --> 00:01:55.328
"The moon doesn't really change shape, you know.

31
00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:58.550
The sun lights up the moon's surface.

32
00:01:59.811 --> 00:02:05.376
As the moon orbits around Earth, the amount of the sunlit surface we can see changes.

33
00:02:06.597 --> 00:02:08.858
These changes are the phases of the moon."

34
00:02:08.878 --> 00:02:11.941
"Aha," Pedro said.

35
00:02:11.961 --> 00:02:15.424
"How long does it take for the moon to orbit Earth?"

36
00:02:15.444 --> 00:02:20.788
"About four weeks—one lunar month," Luna said.

37
00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:25.032
"Oh. Is tonight the start of a lunar month?"

38
00:02:26.452 --> 00:02:31.153
"Nope! The full moon is halfway through a lunar month," Luna explained.

39
00:02:31.173 --> 00:02:35.334
"The new moon is the start of a lunar month.

40
00:02:36.315 --> 00:02:38.055
But it's a confusing name."

41
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:40.956
"Why?" Pedro asked.

42
00:02:40.976 --> 00:02:45.617
"Because that's when the unlit surface of the moon is facing Earth.

43
00:02:46.397 --> 00:02:47.898
We can't see the moon then."

44
00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:51.739
"That should be called a 'no moon' then!"

45
00:02:52.499 --> 00:02:53.459
Pedro grinned.

46
00:02:54.459 --> 00:02:55.380
Luna laughed.

47
00:02:57.904 --> 00:03:02.185
"After a new moon, the moon waxes—or looks like it gets bigger.

48
00:03:03.366 --> 00:03:06.006
A few days later, it's a waxing crescent.

49
00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:10.448
One week after the new moon is the first-quarter moon.

50
00:03:12.128 --> 00:03:15.369
That's when half of the moon's surface is visible from Earth."

51
00:03:15.389 --> 00:03:20.990
"Why is it a quarter moon if half of it is visible?"

52
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:26.192
"Because it's one quarter of the way through the lunar month," Luna said.

53
00:03:27.436 --> 00:03:31.638
"Finally after another week, we have a full moon, like this one.

54
00:03:32.898 --> 00:03:33.879
Are you enjoying it?"

55
00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:37.320
Pedro put his eye to the telescope again.

56
00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:39.621
"It's awesome!"

57
00:03:47.224 --> 00:03:52.747
For the next few nights, Pedro and Luna watched the moon slowly seem to disappear.

58
00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:55.308
"It's waning.

59
00:03:55.744 --> 00:04:00.767
This is a waning gibbous," Luna explained, pointing to the football-shaped moon.

60
00:04:00.787 --> 00:04:05.090
"In a few days, we'll see the third-quarter moon."

61
00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.733
Over a week later it was a new moon, and the sky was moonless.

62
00:04:12.134 --> 00:04:16.797
Soon the moon reappeared, and the waxing moon slowly grew again.

63
00:04:18.397 --> 00:04:22.480
One night, under a full moon, Pedro's mom arrived to pick him up.

64
00:04:26.788 --> 00:04:27.609
"Hey, Pedro!"

65
00:04:27.949 --> 00:04:30.911
Luna called as Pedro put his stuff into Mom's car.

66
00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.874
Luna was holding a big, long box.

67
00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:37.715
"I thought you might like this."

68
00:04:37.735 --> 00:04:42.258
"Whoa! I can't take that," Pedro said.

69
00:04:43.259 --> 00:04:44.360
It was her telescope!

70
00:04:45.541 --> 00:04:46.541
Luna grinned.

71
00:04:46.561 --> 00:04:49.343
"I'm getting a new one soon.

72
00:04:50.264 --> 00:04:51.905
So please take this one."

73
00:04:51.925 --> 00:04:56.108
"Thanks!" Pedro said.

74
00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.842
"That's really generous, Luna.

75
00:05:00.003 --> 00:05:02.144
I'm sorry that I don't have anything for you though."

76
00:05:02.164 --> 00:05:04.326
"That's okay."

77
00:05:05.107 --> 00:05:06.068
Luna smiled.

78
00:05:06.088 --> 00:05:10.932
"Just promise me we can moon-gaze together when I visit the city."

79
00:05:12.213 --> 00:05:13.715
Pedro smiled back.

80
00:05:13.735 --> 00:05:14.856
"Deal!"
